@startuml activity-room-to-match
title Activity: Room-to-Match Lifecycle [C flow / P details / TBD marked]
start
:Host creates room (FR-030);
:Backend generates room code (FR-031);
repeat
  :Players join by code (FR-032)\nas COMPETITOR (max 5, BR-001) or SPECTATOR;
  :Competitors select loadout (FR-040) and mark Ready (FR-035);
repeat while (Host has not pressed Start?) is (waiting) not (Start pressed)
if (all competitors ready AND 2 <= competitors <= 5?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Reject start (409);
  stop
endif
:Backend allocates Match Server from pool;
if (instance available?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :503 NO_SERVER_AVAILABLE, room stays OPEN;
  stop
endif
:Backend issues tickets; clients connect to Match Server;
if (all competitors connected before join timeout?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Apply no-show rule [TBD OQ-GP-06/17];
endif
:PRE_LAUNCH five-second period [semantics TBD OQ-GP-01];
:Launch inputs -> initial spin [formula TBD OQ-GP-02];
:BATTLE: authoritative simulation;
while (competitors remaining >= 2 AND no timeout [TBD]?) is (yes)
  :Simulate tick, send snapshots;
  if (top exits arena?) then (yes)
    :Eliminate (BR-002);\nplayer becomes spectator (BR-004);
  endif
endwhile (no)
:Determine result: winner (BR-003) / draw [TBD];
:Match Server reports result to Backend;
:Backend persists result, history, records;
:Clients show result screen;
if (room persists for rematch? [TBD OQ-GP-14]) then (yes)
  :Room returns to OPEN;
else (no)
  :Room CLOSED;
endif
stop
@enduml
